arm64: dts: rockchip: build the CX3576-Z device tree

kernel/dts/rk3576-cx3576z.dts is this board's maintained device tree and the
Makefile in the pinned Armbian tree does not know about it. Registering it is
what makes `make rockchip/rk3576-cx3576z.dtb` produce anything.

A patch states this edit where every other source change to this tree is
stated -- reviewable in a diff, applied by the same series with the same reject
handling -- instead of an `echo ... >> arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile`
between two build steps, whose failure mode is an append that silently lands in
the wrong file.

The line goes with the other `dtb-` entries rather than after `subdir-y`. The
variable is accumulated, so the built dtb is the same either way.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
@@ -464,6 +464,7 @@
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3576-recomputer-rk3576-devkit.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3576-recomputer-rk3576-module-devkit.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3588-recomputer-rk3588-devkit.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP) += rk3576-cx3576z.dtb
 subdir-y := $(dts-dirs) overlay
 
 # Armbian: Incremental: assuming overlay targets are already in the Makefile
